    "390": {
      "date": "2026-11-10",
      "edition": "Tuesday 10 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Wallabies form",
          "heading": "Australia's 45-22 Twickenham defeat leaves Scotland facing a fairer fight",
          "body": "England beat Australia 45-22 at Twickenham, and Planet Rugby's post-match column suggests Scotland's next opponents are more vulnerable than the scoreline alone implies. The writer describes a team with a \"revolving cast\" at fly-half, porous defence and an inability to control possession. Captain Harry Wilson said England \"put us under the pump, we didn't get too much ball in the first half.\" The column argues the pressure will eventually fall on new coach Les Kiss, whose squad has too many players short of Test standard."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "South Africa beat Italy 66-7",
