      "edition": "Tuesday 10 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Rivalry record",
          "heading": "Steve Tandy's Wales have beaten Japan twice since July 2025",
          "body": "Wales have won two of the three meetings since July 2025, and the Cardiff win a year ago, sealed by Jarrod Evans' last-second penalty, gave head coach Steve Tandy his first Test victory. Wales have never lost in Cardiff against Japan, a record Saturday's 28-21 result left intact. Tandy wants Wales to 'kick on faster', pointing to four victories in 13 matches as the turnaround."
        },
        {
